      "description": "The meme contains harmful content that can be damaging to individuals' self-esteem and perpetuates negative stereotypes about gender and appearance. It promotes objectification and reinforces stereotypes that devalue individuals based on their appearance or sexual appeal, rather than their character or achievements.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_4c526b85"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2824f6c0",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals who are familiar with internet meme culture, particularly those who understand and engage with the phrase 'when nobody knew who you were until you got on your knees.' This includes online audiences who appreciate or consume humor that relies on objectification, gendered stereotypes, and the mocking of public figures for perceived lack of prior recognition or status. The meme is designed to resonate with users who find humor in the idea that someone's value is derived solely from their physical appearance or sexual appeal, and who are comfortable with or perpetuate harmful stereotypes about gender roles and objectification.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_4c526b85"
      },
